# 🌍 7. CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL (EXPOSE TO INTERNET)

## ▶ Quick tunnel (temporary)

```bash id="cmd17"
cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:5000
```

### What happens:

* creates public URL
* forwards internet → your laptop

---

## ▶ Named tunnel (production-style)

### Login

```bash id="cmd18"
cloudflared tunnel login
```

### Create tunnel

```bash id="cmd19"
cloudflared tunnel create electro-api
```

### Config file

```bash id="cmd20"
nano ~/.cloudflared/config.yml
```

```yaml id="cmd21"
tunnel: TUNNEL_ID
credentials-file: /home/abdo/.cloudflared/TUNNEL_ID.json

ingress:
  - service: http://localhost:5000
  - service: http_status:404
```

### Run tunnel

```bash id="cmd22"
cloudflared tunnel run electro-api
```

---

# 🔁 8. RUN CLOUD TUNNEL IN BACKGROUND (SYSTEMD)

### Create service

```bash id="cmd23"
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/cloudflared-electro.service
```

### Service config

```ini id="cmd24"
ExecStart=/usr/bin/cloudflared tunnel run electro-api
Restart=always
User=abdo
```

### Enable

```bash id="cmd25"
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable cloudflared-electro
sudo systemctl start cloudflared-electro
```

